WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
All right, Tom.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.983
Good to see you.

00:00:02.897 --> 00:00:03.980
Let me get this straight.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.000
Extreme pumpkin carving
is pumpkin carving using,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.820
basically, machinery
that could kill somebody.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:10.653
Is that right?

00:00:10.653 --> 00:00:11.486
That's basically it.

00:00:11.486 --> 00:00:13.830
And this is to get the job
done quickly, more efficiently.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:14.663
Is that right?

00:00:14.663 --> 00:00:15.496
That's right.

00:00:15.496 --> 00:00:16.329
'Cause I'm lazy.

00:00:16.329 --> 00:00:17.162
Okay, you're lazy.

00:00:17.162 --> 00:00:19.180
Well, no joke, I did a pumpkin
for my daughter last night.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.570
It took about two and
half hours to carve it up.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.290
I was bruised and beaten at the end.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:24.525
So, this is definitely the way to go.

00:00:24.525 --> 00:00:25.358
Is that right?

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:26.210
Yeah, you can't let the pumpkins win.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.300
You gotta get to 'em.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.939
Can't let the pumpkins win.

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:29.772
(audience laughs)

00:00:29.772 --> 00:00:31.850
That's a great motto for Halloween.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:33.250
Those bastards have to die.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.350
All right, why don't you start us off?

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:36.710
Tell us, what's the first thing to do?

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:38.960
Well, the first thing is to
take the top off the pumpkin,

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.363
so I use this thing, a reciprocator.

00:00:40.363 --> 00:00:42.587
I see that you're wearing
safety equipment and I am not.

00:00:42.587 --> 00:00:44.530
So, I should probably put
on these goggles right here.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:45.424
Is that correct?

00:00:45.424 --> 00:00:46.310
That's probably a good idea, yeah.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:47.810
And you're using a reciprocating saw?

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:48.643
Yep.

00:00:48.643 --> 00:00:50.778
So, I jab it in there like this.

00:00:50.778 --> 00:00:51.736
Pull the trigger.

00:00:51.736 --> 00:00:54.403
(machine whirs)

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.150
Okay, I don't even see
what saw that is over here.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.461
I don't even know how to do that.

00:01:00.461 --> 00:01:01.294
It's this one here?

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.600
I don't even know how to turn it on.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.433
Thumb on that one.

00:01:03.433 --> 00:01:05.020
I'm so scared.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:05.853
Oh, there we go, right?

00:01:05.853 --> 00:01:06.856
Like that?

00:01:06.856 --> 00:01:08.227
Just squeeze it.

00:01:08.227 --> 00:01:10.606
And then you just put this in here?

00:01:10.606 --> 00:01:12.356
And then just make a?

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.003
Okay, that's a mess.

00:01:16.958 --> 00:01:18.690
All right, so once you take the top.

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.500
This is much easier than
what I did last night,

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.910
and it's making a lot
more noise which is cool.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:25.200
Would you recommend for people
to do this in there house?

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.480
Like, with kids around?

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.630
[Tom] Maybe outdoors.

00:01:28.686 --> 00:01:31.468
(Conan grunts)

00:01:31.468 --> 00:01:33.089
Here we go, all right.

00:01:33.089 --> 00:01:34.220
There.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:35.131
Good enough.

00:01:35.131 --> 00:01:36.430
(audience laughs)

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:37.520
Okay, so then what?

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.530
Another tool I use is a
drill for doing, like,

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.795
nostril and things like that.

00:01:41.795 --> 00:01:43.150
What does that do?

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:44.543
Just making holes.

00:01:46.496 --> 00:01:47.480
There you go.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.724
You got that one.

00:01:48.724 --> 00:01:51.224
(drill whirs)

00:01:55.735 --> 00:01:58.568
(audience laughs)

00:02:01.768 --> 00:02:02.685
Use mine.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.554
And by the way, there's a kind of,

00:02:05.554 --> 00:02:07.140
it's exciting to do that.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.016
It feels good.

00:02:08.016 --> 00:02:09.410
Yeah, you're winning!

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:10.243
You're winning!

00:02:10.243 --> 00:02:11.510
The pumpkin is like, "No, no!"

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:13.584
And I'm like, "Yeah, yeah!"

00:02:13.584 --> 00:02:14.417
Spank it!

00:02:14.417 --> 00:02:15.330
Well, don't get crazy.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.197
That's just sexual.

00:02:16.197 --> 00:02:17.170
All right, let's go.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.880
Another tool I use is this thing.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:19.713
What is that?

00:02:19.713 --> 00:02:20.546
What does that do?

00:02:20.546 --> 00:02:21.930
I call it a pumpkin gooper.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:22.763
I made you one.

00:02:22.763 --> 00:02:24.270
Check yours out.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.103
Oh my.

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:25.936
Oh, that's sweet.

00:02:25.936 --> 00:02:27.110
Look at my pumpkin gooper right there.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.540
It looks like his head.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.373
[Conan] You see that?

00:02:29.373 --> 00:02:30.206
Yeah, it's got a little.

00:02:30.206 --> 00:02:32.030
And that goes in there and just.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.610
You whip it around like that.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:34.443
Give it a try.

00:02:34.443 --> 00:02:36.200
So, this is what takes the longest time,

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.100
is scooping the goop out
of the empty pumpkin.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.211
So, you're saying you put this.

00:02:41.211 --> 00:02:44.044
(audience laughs)

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:48.850
That's pretty good.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.003
You have to hold me while I do it.

00:02:52.398 --> 00:02:55.065
(machine whirs)

00:02:59.536 --> 00:03:02.369
(audience groans)

00:03:04.218 --> 00:03:05.889
Can't let the pumpkins win.

00:03:05.889 --> 00:03:07.040
You can't let the pumpkins win.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.210
This is America after all.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:09.270
Okay.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:10.320
Wanna do one more?

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.660
I wanna do a lot more!

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:14.570
All right, let's grab that
pumpkin over there on the edge.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:15.854
Okay, this one here.

00:03:15.854 --> 00:03:17.322
We're gonna use a chainsaw.

00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:18.500
A chainsaw?

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.380
Yeah.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.626
I never used a chainsaw before.

00:03:20.626 --> 00:03:21.680
Well, that'll go well.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:22.538
In my life.

00:03:22.538 --> 00:03:24.370
(audience laughs)

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.390
You could probably tell just

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.840
by how I've handled things so far.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:27.970
The chainsaw's right over here.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.850
It's the thing with the chain on it.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:30.762
Thanks, pal.

00:03:30.762 --> 00:03:31.595
(audience laughs)

00:03:31.595 --> 00:03:34.222
Thanks for making me look even wussier.

00:03:34.222 --> 00:03:35.055
There ya go.

00:03:35.055 --> 00:03:36.010
Whoa, what are we doing with this?

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.262
Just take a chunk off of this side.

00:03:38.262 --> 00:03:39.095
Off this side?

00:03:39.095 --> 00:03:39.928
Like this.

00:03:39.928 --> 00:03:42.678
(chainsaw whirs)

00:03:48.598 --> 00:03:51.200
(audience laughs)

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.033
Why did mine?

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.323
Why did mine take so
much longer than yours?

00:03:57.323 --> 00:03:58.560
I picked a good one.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.310
I finished and you were reading a book.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:03.961
And then, we made, like,
Siamese twins out of that.

00:04:03.961 --> 00:04:04.794
See?

00:04:04.794 --> 00:04:07.794
(audience applauds)

00:04:10.194 --> 00:04:11.410
(Conan grunts)

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:13.080
This one just had a lobotomy.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.371
(audience laughs)

00:04:14.371 --> 00:04:15.290
Huh?

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:16.360
You ready for the big stuff?

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:17.193
Oh my God, what is that?

00:04:17.193 --> 00:04:18.026
Tell me what that is?

00:04:18.026 --> 00:04:19.520
Well, I read that the world record

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:22.100
for carving a pumpkin is,
like, 30 seconds or something.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.590
And I said I can do it in
under a minute if I make this.

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:26.210
So, I made you one too right there.

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:27.990
Could you demonstrate
this and then I'll try.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.000
What is this thing called?

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.240
I call it the pumpkin thumper.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:32.880
So, you take a pumpkin like this.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:33.713
Yeah, hold on.

00:04:33.713 --> 00:04:34.546
Let me get out there.

00:04:34.546 --> 00:04:36.970
I'm slipping on pumpkin
intestine over here.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:38.150
And then you take this thing.

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:38.983
Yeah?

00:04:41.363 --> 00:04:42.196
And you whack it.

00:04:42.196 --> 00:04:44.629
Like that.

00:04:44.629 --> 00:04:48.546
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:52.253
Right here?

00:04:52.253 --> 00:04:53.086
Like that?

00:04:53.086 --> 00:04:53.974
Okay.

00:04:53.974 --> 00:04:54.807
You know how to split wood, right?

00:04:54.807 --> 00:04:56.870
Yeah, I split wood all the time!

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.397
What are ya talking about?

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.653
I split wood yesterday!

00:05:00.653 --> 00:05:03.163
With the thing that has the chain on it!

00:05:03.163 --> 00:05:06.520
(audience laughs)

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:07.463
Okay.

00:05:07.463 --> 00:05:10.046
(Conan groans)

00:05:11.852 --> 00:05:13.740
That was too hard.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.508
Yeah, too much muscle.

00:05:15.508 --> 00:05:17.470
(Conan grunts)

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.220
(Conan grunts)

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:20.960
Okay, that was too much.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.170
There ya go.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.003
Try again.

00:05:23.003 --> 00:05:24.583
Right here?

00:05:24.583 --> 00:05:25.416
Okay.

00:05:25.416 --> 00:05:26.249
You gotta get really worked up into a rage

00:05:26.249 --> 00:05:27.971
when you do this, I think.

00:05:27.971 --> 00:05:30.013
Son of a bitch!

00:05:30.013 --> 00:05:32.846
(audience cheers)

00:05:41.604 --> 00:05:44.187
(Conan grunts)

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.230
Ready?

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:49.539
On three.

00:05:49.539 --> 00:05:52.109
One, two, three.

00:05:52.109 --> 00:05:54.692
(Conan grunts)

00:05:55.983 --> 00:05:58.200
Oh, that feels so good!

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.840
(audience laughs)

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:02.889
Okay, I'm having a small series
of heart attacks right now.

00:06:02.889 --> 00:06:04.170
(audience laughs)

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.860
The book is "Extreme Pumpkin Two."

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:07.100
It's in stores now.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:07.933
You're a good man.

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:09.340
Tom Nardone, thank you very much.

